- Added a deterministic regression that fills the ordinary registry to 64 while socket readiness ignores cancellation, initiates transport close before releasing those operations, proves bounded close and exactly one socket close, then proves late readiness performs no bridge read/write and all owned resources eventually return to zero.
- Preserved the adapter-only libssh2/OpenSSL boundary and all four explicit M3-deferred `unsupported`/`notReported` states owned by `TASK-260728-3cveay`; no deferred value is fabricated.

