+# TASK-260715-1ozsb6 reviewer validation — round 9
+
+- `swift test --filter saturatedOrdinaryOperationsCannotSkipSocketClose`: exit 0; 1 test / 1 suite.
+- `swift test --filter LibSSH2`: exit 1; 40 tests / 3 suites, failure at `LibSSH2AdapterIntegrationTests.swift:512` (`nonCooperativeUploadSourceTimeout`).
+- `swift test --filter nonCooperativeUploadSourceTimeout`: exit 0 when rerun alone, confirming an order/concurrency-sensitive failure.
+- `make validate-core`: exit 2; 374 tests / 31 suites, failure at `LibSSH2BridgeTests.swift:211` in `repeatedHandshakeCleanup`, iteration 1: `automaticTasks` was 1 rather than 0 after teardown.
+- `make validate-libssh2`: exit 0.
+- `make test-libssh2-source-gates`: exit 0.
+- `make native-apple-matrix`: exit 0; arm64/x86_64 macOS provider and harness release targets built and linked.
+- `swift-format lint --recursive --strict Package.swift Sources Tests`: exit 0 (`swift-format` 602.0.0).
+- `swift build`: exit 0.
+- `git diff --check`: exit 0.
+- `task-board validate`: exit 0 with the known `STORY-260715-lkshfz` aggregate mismatch while the task is `reviewing`.
+
+Blocking lifecycle evidence: `performTearDown()` can finish while a cooperative reserved timeout race is still registered, and `ownedResourceSnapshot()` counts that registry as `automaticTasks`. In addition, when socket close consumes the transport-close deadline and automatic tasks exist, the automatic-task join branch is skipped and their stored references are never cleared. This prevents deterministic post-close baseline restoration.
